From d85eb97557e328cdd2223d4dbc4ee903c49dc1d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patch <patch@local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 22:24:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] G3e-1 + G3e-2: Level 1->2 subsection grouping + LLM
 relative-placement pool

G3e-1 (eo/mech_subsections.py): deterministic, LLM-free grouping of
mech.placements into Level 2 subsections off G0's existing mount_<id>
sibling convention. Singleton subsections for mount-less parts, orphaned
mounts kept as their own singleton so nothing gets dropped.

G3e-2 (agents/mech_subsection_pool.py): worker-pool LLM fan-out
(role_tag=mech_subsection, same Cerebras pool as mech_primitive) that
proposes each subsection's mount-relative-to-part offset, skipping
subsections already grounded in real mount_spec data
(_resize_mount_parts_from_mount_spec's rect/cc patterns).

eo/registry.py: registers mech_subsection onto the shared Cerebras pool.

Tests: 28 new unit tests, full suite (315) green.
